      "text": [
        "304 - وَ رُوِيَ فِي خَبَرٍ آخَرَ: «أَنَّهُ مَنْ يُقَلِّمْ أَظَافِيرَهُ يَوْمَ اَلْجُمُعَةِ ' يَبْدَأْ بِخِنْصِرِهِ مِنَ اَلْيَدِ اَلْيُسْرَى وَ يَخْتِمْ بِخِنْصِرِهِ مِنَ اَلْيَدِ اَلْيُمْنَى."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.304 - It is also reported in another narration:\n\"Whoever trims their nails on Jumu’ah should start with the little finger of the left hand and finish with the little finger of the right hand.\""
